From: Notebook OS <benwhiting810@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wm: keep the desktop widget column below every window

The Tasks/Calendar desktop widget column is a floating DIALOG (matchbox
force-fullscreens DESKTOP-type windows, so it cannot use that layer). Being a
dialog, matchbox stacked it at the dialog level -- i.e. ABOVE apps, and at the
same level as the Finder -- so a click, a raise, or the race when an app maps
could leave the widget cards rendered in FRONT of a window. The app-side
keep-below / re-lower / hide-when-active hacks could not make this reliable.

stack_get_window_list() is the single choke point that projects matchbox's
internal stack onto the X server. Pin the widget column (a DIALOG whose WM_NAME
is "nb-desktop-widgets") to the very bottom, just above the desktop wallpaper
and below every app and other dialog, so it can never render in front of a
window -- mirroring the panel-above-dialogs rule in 0003.

Signed-off-by: Notebook OS <benwhiting810@gmail.com>
---
 src/stack.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/stack.c b/src/stack.c
--- a/src/stack.c
+++ b/src/stack.c
@@ -215,6 +215,16 @@
     if (!fullscreen_app && c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_PANEL)
       continue;
 
+    /* Notebook OS: hold the desktop wallpaper (DESKTOP) and the desktop widget
+     * column (a DIALOG titled "nb-desktop-widgets") out of the main pass; they
+     * are emitted last, at the very bottom, so the widget column can never be
+     * stacked in front of an app or the Finder. */
+    if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_DESKTOP)
+      continue;
+    if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_DIALOG && c->name
+        && !strcmp((char *)c->name, "nb-desktop-widgets"))
+      continue;
+
     dbg("%i:%li, ", i, c->frame);
 
     win_list[i++] = c->frame;
@@ -227,6 +237,17 @@
 
   }
 
+  /* Notebook OS: emit the desktop widget column just above the wallpaper (below
+   * every app and dialog), then the wallpaper itself at the very bottom. */
+  stack_enumerate_reverse(w, c)
+    if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_DIALOG && c->name
+        && !strcmp((char *)c->name, "nb-desktop-widgets"))
+      win_list[i++] = c->frame;
+
+  stack_enumerate_reverse(w, c)
+    if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_DESKTOP)
+      win_list[i++] = c->frame;
+
   dbg("\n");
 
   return win_list;
